    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d118">

                <pb facs="0206" n="160" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg160"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/2536</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        President Wilson
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 7, 1918</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: Enclosed is a
                    translation of the Austro-Hungarian note handed to me this morning by the
                    Minister of Sweden.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d118-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>It seems to me that the <hi rendition="#underline">offer</hi> to conclude an
                    armistice and enter upon negotiations can only be considered after the
                    Austro-Hungarian Government has accepted unconditionally the principles which
                    you have laid down and after the sincerity of the <hi rendition="#underline"
                        >offer</hi> (which ought to be “request”) is shown by withdrawal from all
                    occupied territory, by denouncement of the treaties of Brest-Litovsk and
                    Bucharest, and by a declaration that these acts will be performed regardless of
                    the course pursued by Germany—that is on the basis of a separate peace.</p>
                <p>The foregoing is a hasty suggestion. I hope we can make speedy answer because of
                    the Loan Campaign.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
